{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"A scene flashes before you. Web is standing in a sewer basin, looking up at someone above them. Through the grate above them you can see a young mousy child doing a small performance with a set of balls. Web smiles, and the figure looks down. \n\"Hello?\" The figure asks.\nWeb pokes their head out of the grate and reaches a hand to shake. \"You're pretty young to be out here alone by yourself. What's your name?\"\n\"My name? Umm, I calls meself Skitter.\"\nMore memories flash by as you watch Web see Skitter grow from a scared street rat to a young man with friends he made himself.\nYou see Web bringing him food so he doesn't go hungry.\nWeb showing Skitter the sewers for the first time, his eyes wide in amazement at the massive farms down below.\nWeb making Skitter a jacket from spider silk and scavenged brown fabric.\nWeb meeting up with Skitter on the rooftops to talk about city life.\nMany late night talks spent up there.\nSkitter's tenth birthday, Web managing to get all the ingredients together to make a small cake.\nThe first time Web met Skitter's mouse friend.\nWeb repairing the jacket after a nasty run-in with the Redcoats. \nWeb finding Skitter beat up one night and nursing him back to health. \nSkitter giving Web a cake they 'acquired' for Web's 18th birthday.\nWeb meeting Skitter's new friends through him. \nWeb giving Skitter's mouse the top hat.\nSkitter telling Web they were a shifter too\nWeb boarding the Tir Na Nog, worried about Skitter making in on board\nWeb starting work on Skitter's binder.\nWeb watching Skitter and Wren dance just hours before.\nInstead of those, Web remembers being alone. Growing up in the sewers with no friends on the surface. \nNever finding anyone like them.\nStill living without ever knowing what they really are.\nBeing scared of never finding someone who understands all they've been through. \nThe Web who knows Skitter grew up loved and accepted, understood for who they were.\nThe Web who has forgotten Skitter had none of those things.","created_at":"2020-07-30T05:12:51.234000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-30T22:11:20.923000Z","id":"738262814489182321","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"There's the full scene thing for thos interested","created_at":"2020-07-30T05:13:02.228000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"738262860601491578","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"mazie","id":"366565198284324868","is_bot":0,"username":"damnzam"},"author_id":"366565198284324868","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"The image is hazy, as if even Vee doesn't recall this scene perfectly. Her memory has been Modified too many times before, but there is always one constant when she starts to recall. \n\nYou see the interior of a shop in a small village just outside of London. There is ash everywhere, and a clearing right where two figures lie. Vee, a few years younger though you're not quite sure how many years exactly. Her hair is shorter ending just around her chin.\n\nVee lies on the floor, cradled in the arms of a man who looks quite similar to her, her brother and last of her family.\n\nThis is Vee's first ever memory. \n\n\"Vee? Vee, wake up.\"\n\nStirring, she does. She opens her mouth, tries to call out for anything, but struggles to remember as it catches in her throat. Remember? Remember anything. She can't even remember how to speak.\n\n\"Viorica.\" He tells her her name. It sounds beautiful. It sounds right. His eyes are blue like the summer sky, against the light of her own green. But his face is hers, and her face is his. Ghosts of her past linger in the back of her head, nameless and faceless and taunting in her dreams; but her past and the emptiness of it do not seem to matter to him.\n\nThe scenes continue in fast-forward, scrubbing away the man from every single one. Teaching her to walk, teaching her to speak. When the summer heat is at its worst, the pair escaping to the woods, or swimming in the nearby muddy creek, or laying for hours in the meadow they call theirs, watching the sun pass from overhead. All of them memories from a face too much like her own... but a name she will no longer place.\n\nSeeing these memories again, for what is going to be the last time, for this split second, Vee feels infinite, she is everywhere. For this split second, she remembers it all.\n\nAnd then she breaks into a million pieces, and only one comes back. Hollow and incomplete, but she is back. She is here and alive. And the split second is over, and she can't remember anymore.","created_at":"2020-07-30T05:25:48.261000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-30T05:36:36.100000Z","id":"738266073576505375","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
