{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"izar","id":"566079740591603714","is_bot":0,"username":"izarsystem"},"author_id":"566079740591603714","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"Arc has carved and painted a glowing star chart into the bottom of Cato's old bunk (the surface above them)","created_at":"2020-07-30T07:15:05.937000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"738293578463313952","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Basil","id":"339235123759153162","is_bot":0,"username":"divinedefault"},"author_id":"339235123759153162","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"Somewhere in the world, but not on the sub, a brass dragonborne sings:\n\"Think of me not, as a hero or a star.\nRemember me a stranger who had come from very far.\nThink of me not, as a man who filled your dreams.\nRemember me as a hand to hold and smile always beemed\n\nThink of not our strifes, but forget not of our fights.\nRemember all the times even when I was unright.\nThink not of my troubles, remember not my pain.\nEvery while I made you smile shall be my new refrain.\n\nThink of not your road ahead, i'll be not far behind. Remember me as thus, i'm at home inside your mind.\n\nRemember me thus, as one who made you grin\nRemember me thus, i'm happy here within\nRemember me thus, the one who loved so meek\nRemember thus, you inspired this freak\"","created_at":"2020-07-30T22:09:47.290000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"738518734377058375","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"\"I was curious. Why was he smashing all those beetles? What did he get out of it? First thing I did was ask him. “Orson, why are you smashing all those beetles?” He gave me an answer. “Smash the beetles! Smash them! Kun kun kun!” I wasn’t deterred. I was the smartest person I knew; certainly I had the wherewithal to unravel the mysteries that lay at the heart of a moron. So I went to Maester Valeric’s library.\"","created_at":"2020-07-30T23:36:24.452000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"738540532854161478","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"\"I know, I know, but still it filled me with dread. Piles and piles of them, years and years of them. How many countless living, crawling things smashed, dried out, and returned to the dirt? In my dreams, I found myself standing on a beach made of beetle husks stretching as far as the eye can see. I woke up, crying, weeping for their shattered little bodies. I tried to stop Orson once.\"","created_at":"2020-07-30T23:36:57.441000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"738540671220056124","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"Tyrion Lannister:\nHe just pushed me aside with a “kun”, kept on smashing. Every day. Until that mule kicked him in the chest and killed him. [Tyrion releases the bug and it crawls away] So what do you think? Why did he do it? What’s it all about?\n\nJaime Lannister:\nI don’t know. [the bells toll, signaling the time is approaching; Jaime stands and walks to the door of the cell] Good luck today.","created_at":"2020-07-30T23:37:35.328000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"738540830129782895","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
